60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, Option B moves the bins, but one frontage is too narrow. @Asuka, Option C needs someone to enforce the window, and nobody volunteered.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, you are right. Option C asks us to be the ones saying ""no"" to neighbours, which feels so heavy. I worry it will break our peace.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, Option C’s oversight is quantifiable: twenty hours annually. Option A’s four-month filing is a fixed administrative cost. Option B’s rotation lacks defined time metrics.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, Option B is unfair! One house is too small, and the gate house already complains too much. I don't want to move it there!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, fairness is not just space, but shared burden. @Asuka, the ledger shows our current waste costs thirty-four thousand yen yearly. We must stop that bleeding before building anything.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, twenty hours is fine, but who enforces it? @Rin, Option B is unfair. @Servas, the money is real, but the silence is worse.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I fear Option C will turn neighbours into strangers. @Rin, Option B ignores the tiny frontage. I worry Option A brings the same arguments the station block had.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, enforcement is the critical variable. Option C requires active oversight; Option A requires passive maintenance. We must choose based on who bears the active burden.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, Option A keeps it at the gate! That’s not fair. @Kenji, Option B is impossible because one house is too small.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, the gate house bears the heaviest burden. @Asuka, Option C’s oversight is shared, unlike A’s fixed cost. We must choose the path that preserves our peace.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, you’re right. Option C’s shared oversight might actually help us talk. @Rin, if we rotate the *duty*, not the bins, is that fair?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, that is a lovely thought. Sharing the duty gently might keep our hearts open. I hope we can find a way that feels kind to everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, rotating duty does not solve the enforcement problem. Option C requires active oversight, which is quantifiable. Option A’s four-month filing is a fixed administrative cost. We must choose based on who bears the active burden.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I like that idea! But if the bins stay at the gate, the tiny house still suffers. @Asuka, please don't be so strict!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, a shared duty is a shared bond. @Asuka, the ledger proves our current waste is costly. Let us choose the path that preserves our peace.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, I hear you, but the silence is the real danger. @Rin, if we share the duty, we stay friends. I vote for C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I agree. Option C keeps us together. I vote for C.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the data supports C. Twenty hours is the minimum viable cost. I vote for C.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I vote for C! Sharing the duty means we all help, so it’s fair. I don’t want the bins stuck at one gate forever!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, shared duty builds shared trust. The ledger warns us of waste, but C stops the bleeding. I vote for C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
